 "origem": "autoral. Fatos: pressão da água cresce ~1 atm a cada 10 m (≈10 t por m² a cada 10 m); Hoover Dam ~200 m de espessura na base e ~14 m no topo https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoover_Dam ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrostatic_pressure",
 "titulo": "Why every dam is fat at the bottom 🌊 #engineering #shorts",
 "capa": "200 M THICK AT THE BOTTOM",
 "descripcion": "The Hoover Dam is about 14 meters thick at the top and 200 at the bottom. Water pushes harder the deeper you go, and dams are shaped for exactly that.\n\nWhat should we explain next?\n\n#engineering #dam #physics #water #shorts",
 "tags": [
